id: pm-ygerpy
title: "GH-802: persist structured numeric measurements with test runs"
description: "Linked verification records whether a run passed but cannot persist what it measured, forcing coverage, latency, bundle-size, error-budget, and duplication values into unqueryable prose."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:cli","area:sdk",context-management,gh-issue,linked-tests,metrics,queryability
created_at: "2026-07-29T02:35:07.399Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T05:58:27.430Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-29T05:56:00.631Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-29T05:56:00.631Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Test-run records accept typed numeric measurements with a name, value, optional unit, optional threshold, and timestamp without requiring an extension; Measurements remain bound to the producing run and accumulate as a bounded deterministic series rather than overwriting prior evidence; CLI, SDK, MCP, schemas, contracts, storage normalization, migrations, and public types expose the same measurement model; Read surfaces can filter and aggregate measurements, including a metric-below query and a latest-versus-previous diff; Focused, integration, acceptance, compatibility, and exact 100 percent coverage gates prove persistence and query behavior"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make quantitative verification evidence a first-class queryable SDK primitive
value: Agents and fleet operators can compare quality evidence without parsing prose
impact: Adds a universal numeric evidence series usable by any project domain while retaining bounded item storage
outcome: "Quality, performance, reliability, and size measurements are durable, attributable, and queryable across items"
why_now: GH-802 documents 18 package baselines currently stranded in prose despite test-result tracking being enabled
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
repro_steps: "Enable test-result-tracking, run a linked verification that emits a coverage or latency value, inspect the persisted item, then attempt to filter items by that value."
resolution: "Test runs now persist bounded typed measurements with SDK parsing, threshold queries, diffs, and CLI/MCP contract parity."
expected_result: "A test run can carry structured numeric evidence that list, aggregate, and diff surfaces can query."
actual_result: Current test_runs store status and counts only; measured baselines must be embedded in prose.
affected_version: 2026.7.29
component: sdk-test-result-model
customer_impact: Fleet-wide quality baselines cannot currently drive prioritization or trend analysis through pm.
